  {
   "id": 32,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -1560,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 31,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "INSANE MOTION CONTROL \u2014 Wan 2.2 Fun-Control (native nodes)\n\nWHAT THIS DOES\nAnimates YOUR character with motion taken from a reference clip.\nDWPose extracts a pose skeleton from the motion video; Wan 2.2\nFun-Control renders your character following that exact motion.\nIdentity comes from the character reference image (+ optional\ncharacter LoRA added after the UNET loaders).\n\nQUICK START\n1) INPUTS group: upload character_reference.png (clean, well-lit,\n   framing similar to the motion clip) and motion_reference.mp4.\n2) Positive prompt: describe character, outfit, scene, camera \u2014\n   AND describe the motion in words. It helps adherence.\n3) Queue. Output \u2192 output/insane_motion/.\n\nDEFAULTS = MAX QUALITY (20 steps, cfg 3.5).\n~8\u201312 min per 5 s clip on A100 80GB @ 720p with sage attention.\nFor 10\u00d7 faster drafts see note \u2462 QUALITY VS SPEED.\n\nThe bottom group is a plain Image-to-Video branch (no pose\ncontrol), muted by default \u2014 see note \u2464."
   ],
   "title": "\u2460 READ ME \u2014 INSANE MOTION CONTROL",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 33,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -1040,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 32,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "REQUIRED FILES \u2014 download_models.sh fetches everything.\n\ndiffusion_models/\n  wan2.2_fun_control_high_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors\n  wan2.2_fun_control_low_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors\n  wan2.2_i2v_high_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors  (alt branch)\n  wan2.2_i2v_low_noise_14B_fp8_scaled.safetensors   (alt branch)\ntext_encoders/umt5_xxl_fp8_e4m3fn_scaled.safetensors\nvae/wan_2.1_vae.safetensors\nloras/wan2.2_t2v_A14b_{high,low}_noise_..._4step_1217.safetensors\nloras/wan2.2_i2v_lightx2v_4steps_lora_v1_{high,low}_noise.safetensors\n\nDWPose (yolox_l + dw-ll torchscript) and RIFE (rife49.pth)\nauto-download on the FIRST queue \u2014 the first run is slower.\n\nWHY TWO DIFFUSION MODELS?\nWan 2.2 A14B is a two-expert MoE: the HIGH-noise expert lays out\nmotion + composition (steps 0\u201310), the LOW-noise expert refines\ndetail (10\u201320). Keep pairs matched: high\u2192high, low\u2192low. The two\nsamplers below implement exactly this split."
   ],
   "title": "\u2461 MODELS",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 34,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    -520,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 33,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "PRESET A \u2014 MAX QUALITY (current defaults; use for finals)\n  Lightning LoRA nodes: BYPASSED (purple)\n  HIGH sampler: steps 20 \u00b7 cfg 3.5 \u00b7 start 0 \u00b7 end 10\n  LOW  sampler: steps 20 \u00b7 cfg 3.5 \u00b7 start 10 \u00b7 end 10000\n  ModelSampling shift (both): 8.0\n  A100 80GB @ 1280\u00d7720\u00d781f: \u2248 8\u201312 min\n\nPRESET B \u2014 LIGHTNING (drafts / iteration, \u224810\u00d7 faster)\n  Select both \u26a1 LoRA nodes \u2192 Ctrl+B to activate\n  HIGH sampler: steps 4 \u00b7 cfg 1.0 \u00b7 start 0 \u00b7 end 2\n  LOW  sampler: steps 4 \u00b7 cfg 1.0 \u00b7 start 2 \u00b7 end 10000\n  ModelSampling shift (both): 5.0\n  A100 @ 720p: \u2248 60\u2013120 s\n\nIterate with B, then render the final with A (same seed).\nLightning trades some motion nuance + texture for speed.\nThis Fun-Control branch uses the t2v-based 4-step LoRAs;\nthe I2V branch pairs with the i2v_..._v1 LoRAs instead."
   ],
   "title": "\u2462 QUALITY VS SPEED",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 35,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    0,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 34,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "\u2022 force_rate 16 + frame_load_cap 81 \u2192 exactly 81 frames = 5.0 s.\n  Longer clips get cut \u2014 trim to the exact move you want.\n\u2022 Match framing: full-body motion clip \u2192 full-body character\n  reference. Mismatched crops are the #1 cause of warped anatomy.\n\u2022 ONE person in the motion clip; clean background helps DWPose.\n\u2022 DWPose resolution 1024 is a good ceiling. If the skeleton\n  flickers frame-to-frame, drop to 512.\n\u2022 Vertical video (Reels): swap W/H to 720\u00d71280 in BOTH ImageScale\n  nodes AND the Fun-Control node.\n\u2022 Drafts: 832\u00d7480 runs ~3\u00d7 faster; upscale winners later.\n\u2022 RIFE doubles 16\u219232 fps. For 24 fps deliverables: multiplier 3\n  (\u219248 fps) + frame_rate 48, or remove RIFE and export at 16.\n\nUse motion clips you have the rights to, driving YOUR original\ncharacter \u2014 this rig is not for replicating real people."
   ],
   "title": "\u2463 MOTION REFERENCE TIPS",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 36,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    520,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 35,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "The bottom group is plain Wan 2.2 Image-to-Video: no pose\ncontrol, the model invents motion from your start image + prompt.\nUse it when you have no motion reference, or for subtle idle /\nb-roll / ambient shots.\n\nENABLE: drag-select every node in the bottom group \u2192 Ctrl+M.\nWhile testing it, mute the Fun-Control samplers (same trick)\nso you don't render both branches per queue.\n\nSame two presets apply. For Lightning here, insert\nLoraLoaderModelOnly nodes with the i2v_lightx2v_4steps_v1\nhigh/low LoRAs after each UNET loader.\n\nPrompt tip: describe the motion explicitly and keep camera verbs\nsimple \u2014 'slow dolly-in', 'gentle handheld sway', 'hair moving\nin the wind'."
   ],
   "title": "\u2464 ALT BRANCH \u2014 PURE I2V (muted)",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
  {
   "id": 37,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    1040,
    -620
   ],
   "size": [
    480,
    520
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 36,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "BEST IDENTITY RESULTS\nBuild a perfect character still FIRST in\ninsane_image_to_image.json (PuLID + character LoRA + upscale),\nthen feed that render in here as character_reference.png.\nThe video model can only hold an identity as well as the\nreference you hand it.\n\nLONGER CLIPS\nGenerate 5 s segments; use the last frame of segment N as the\nreference for segment N+1; concat afterwards (ffmpeg). Expect\nslight identity drift \u2014 re-anchor with your best still every\n2\u20133 segments.\n\nCHARACTER LORA (optional, strongest identity lock)\nTrain a Wan 2.2 LoRA on 20\u201350 stills of your character (the\nimg2img workflow is the still-factory), then add\nLoraLoaderModelOnly after BOTH UNET loaders, strength 0.6\u20130.9.\nStack order: UNET \u2192 character LoRA \u2192 Lightning LoRA \u2192 shift."
   ],
   "title": "\u2465 SYSTEM SYNERGY",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
 ],
